{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790682565,"nonce":"HlO5vXKr/0JwJr77LVyW9wkORGg=","message":"Implemented the first language-neutral Rayzor seam.\n\n- `xgpu-bindgen::generate_rayzor` now emits the typed xgpu model, exact `rayzor::gpu` method descriptors, and runtime symbol registration from the same declaration.\n- Generated C wrappers normalize xgpu's internal `i32`/`f32` types to Rayzor's `i64`/`f64` plugin ABI. This avoids relying on native register coercion and prepares the path for wasm's exact function signatures.\n- Rayzor's plugin/runtime now expose pending/resolve/reject completion for native callback futures. Rejection copies UTF-8 and creates the language exception only on the awaiting thread; first completion wins.\n- Rayzor's native method macro now counts all parameter arities supported by its 16-slot descriptor.\n- xgpu's backend exposes cloned device, queue and buffer access plus buffer insertion for Rayzor-owned shader and compute extensions.\n\nValidated with the xgpu workspace, a standalone generated-adapter type-check, Caribou's eight GPU tests, and Rayzor's focused Future/plugin tests.\n\nRemaining adapter work is intentionally in this issue: implement Rayzor Text/Bytes/error/root carriers, include the generated model in `gpu`, merge its descriptors/symbols with the existing package table, and migrate the current compute `GpuBuffer` object to the shared xgpu handle identity before shipping generated externs.","files":null}]}